    },
    {
      kind: 'exercise',
      id: 'ex2.five-number',
      exKind: 'write_code',
      required: true,
      prompt: {
        ar: 'ملخص القمم الخمس بلغة بايثون خالصة (cfds وmedian_of جاهزان): احسب lo = وسيط النصف الأدنى cfds[:n//2]، وmed = وسيط الكل، وhi = وسيط النصف الأعلى cfds[n//2+1:] (لأن n فردي)، ثم iqr = hi − lo، والسورين lo − 1.5×iqr وhi + 1.5×iqr، وقائمة outliers بالقيم خارج السورين. اطبع ثمانية أسطر بهذه الصيغ حرفيًا: min: %d وQ1: %s وmedian: %s وQ3: %s وmax: %d وIQR: %s وfence: %s %s وoutliers: %s. المتوقع: min: 2 / Q1: 5 / median: 8 / Q3: 12 / max: 23 / IQR: 7 / fence: -5.5 22.5 / outliers: [23].',
        en: 'The five-number summary in pure Python (cfds and median_of are given): compute lo = median of the lower half cfds[:n//2], med = median of everything, hi = median of the upper half cfds[n//2+1:] (n is odd), then iqr = hi - lo, the two fences lo - 1.5*iqr and hi + 1.5*iqr, and an outliers list of values beyond the fences. Print exactly eight lines: min: %d, Q1: %s, median: %s, Q3: %s, max: %d, IQR: %s, fence: %s %s, outliers: %s. Expected: min: 2 / Q1: 5 / median: 8 / Q3: 12 / max: 23 / IQR: 7 / fence: -5.5 22.5 / outliers: [23].',
      },
      starterCode: "def median_of(xs):\n    s = sorted(xs)\n    n = len(s)\n    mid = n // 2\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        return s[mid]\n    return (s[mid - 1] + s[mid]) / 2\n\ncfds = [2, 4, 5, 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 12, 14, 23]\nn = len(cfds)\n\n# lo وmed وhi ثم iqr والسورين ثم outliers\n# lo, med, hi, then iqr, both fences, then outliers\n",
      solution: "def median_of(xs):\n    s = sorted(xs)\n    n = len(s)\n    mid = n // 2\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        return s[mid]\n    return (s[mid - 1] + s[mid]) / 2\n\ncfds = [2, 4, 5, 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 12, 14, 23]\nn = len(cfds)\nlo = median_of(cfds[:n // 2])\nmed = median_of(cfds)\nhi = median_of(cfds[n // 2 + 1:])\niqr = hi - lo\nlower_fence = lo - 1.5 * iqr\nupper_fence = hi + 1.5 * iqr\noutliers = []\nfor v in cfds:\n    if v < lower_fence or v > upper_fence:\n        outliers.append(v)\nprint('min: %d' % cfds[0])\nprint('Q1: %s' % lo)\nprint('median: %s' % med)\nprint('Q3: %s' % hi)\nprint('max: %d' % cfds[-1])\nprint('IQR: %s' % iqr)\nprint('fence: %s %s' % (lower_fence, upper_fence))\nprint('outliers: %s' % outliers)",
      tests: [
        {
          id: 't1',
